capital.sensible_book:
Definition for this market: a single-instrument book (Nikkei 225), or at most a two-leg book (Nikkei vs TOPIX), sized in 1-contract steps, with:
- a stop-loss risk per trade of 2% of capital or less (aim for 1-2%);
- at least 2-3 size steps so a volatility forecast can scale exposure;
- margin use of 25-30% of capital or less, leaving room for a limit move (8%) and a margin call.

Risk assumption: daily sigma 1.2-1.6% (long-run TOPIX futures volatility 18.7%/yr, 1976-2009, per Moskowitz-Ooi-Pedersen 2012; Nikkei is typically somewhat higher). On that basis, 1 micro moves about JPY 4.8-6.4k per daily sigma at L = 40,000, or JPY 6.6-8.8k at L = 55,000. A 1.5-sigma stop is about JPY 8-13k per micro.

brokers.eligibility:
A v20 token requires all of:
- an NY-server Pro-course account;
- at least ¥250,000 in that single account;
- Gold status: prior-month volume of at least US$500,000, counting both opens and closes.

New accounts get Gold until the end of the following month. The status system was revamped on 2025-04-01 (5 tiers). The MT5 API needs only an open account.
